Surface nature:  CONTROLLED, storage-agnostic PRESENTATIONAL primitive. The web source's own preamble states it
                 is "deliberately storage-agnostic — DataTable owns the `localStorage` round-trip and feeds us
                 the current `layout` + a controlled `onChange`." It receives the columns + layout as plain
                 props and renders an icon-button trigger + popover; there is NO fetch, NO React-Query cache, NO
                 Promise. So it has NO loading / error / stale / offline branch (nothing to fetch, fail, age, or
                 disconnect). Reproduced branches = the source's REAL ones: closed (only the trigger renders),
                 open with one+ column rows (each visible/hidden via its checkbox, reorderable via ↑/↓ with
                 disabled ends, with the per-row guardrails: required column pinned, last visible column can't be
                 hidden), and the empty column set (web renders an empty list; natively a friendly empty body,
                 never a blank box). No loading/error/stale/offline chrome was fabricated — same faithful-parity
                 stance as the immediately preceding sibling primitive ContextMenu (0206). Browser facilities map
                 to native peers: the controlled `layout`+`onChange` -> @Observable DataTableColumnMenuController
                 owning the layout and mirroring changes to a host callback; the `open` useState + click-outside/
                 Escape dismiss -> .popover with .presentationCompactAdaptation(.popover); <input type=checkbox>
                 -> a HIG checkbox Toggle (ColumnVisibilityToggleStyle); the ↑/↓ keyboard reorder fallback ->
                 labelled step Buttons driven by the pure projector; lib/columnOrderStore -> ColumnLayoutProjector.

